<edge source="mideast_houthi_campaign::armed_offense_rate" target="china_eu_auto_rivalry::supply_chain_integration" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained tempo of missile/drone strikes against ports and transshipment hubs prompts automakers and tier suppliers to accelerate de-risking (nearshoring/dual-sourcing), lowering China–EU component interdependence.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_houthi_campaign::armed_offense_rate" target="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A higher tempo of missile, drone and small-boat offensive strikes directed by non-state actors in the theatre results in more direct incidents against commercial shipping (strikes, attempted boardings, escorts fired upon) in adjacent sea lanes, raising recorded maritime attack frequency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_diesel</data>
</edge>
