  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in available energy (e.g., fuel shortages or disrupted gas flows) raises near‑term inflation expectations and sovereign risk premia, prompting investors to demand higher long‑term yields as compensation for supply‑shock and fiscal stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_west_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_ai</data>
</edge>
