  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained decline in cross-border auto FDI and joint ventures reduces available channels and partners for automotive-tech financing, causing venture and corporate investors in affected markets to cut back on new allocations including to AI projects, lowering AI-specific investment flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_ai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_eu_auto_rivalry::cross_border_investment" target="mideast_houthi_campaign::armed_offense_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased China/EU auto investment in MENA production and parts hubs raises commercial shipping and high-value logistics transiting the Red Sea/Bab al‑Mandeb, expanding the number and attractiveness of maritime and port targets that the Houthi campaign hits with missiles and drones.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
