<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="china_eu_auto_rivalry::vehicle_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising hostile incidents against commercial shipping increase insurance premiums, require rerouting and cause delays, directly reducing the feasible and cost-effective volume of vehicles and powertrains shipped between China and Europe.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="china_eu_auto_rivalry::cross_border_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in maritime attack risk raise expected transport interruptions and costs, incentivizing automakers to commit capital to build or expand production assets closer to target markets (higher foreign direct investment in local plants) rather than rely on long-distance shipments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="global_financial_ai::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in attacks on commercial shipping raises trade disruption risk and market volatility, causing investors and corporate balance sheets to defer or reduce higher‑risk AI project funding.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_ai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="mideast_houthi_campaign::armed_offense_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher rates of successful or visible maritime attacks lower the perceived costs and demonstrate tactics/munitions, encouraging Houthi planners to increase the tempo of missile and drone strikes against regional targets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="mideast_houthi_campaign::defensive_response_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in attacks on commercial shipping prompts regional states and coalition navies/air forces to increase patrols, interdictions, and kinetic responses against groups conducting those attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_diesel::shipping_attack_frequenc" target="mideast_houthi_campaign::aviation_service_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising maritime attacks—especially those involving rockets/drones or proximate to busy air corridors—raise safety and insurance assessments, causing carriers and regulators to curtail or reroute flights and reduce service levels in the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_diesel</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
</edge>
