<edge source="global_financial_ai::bond_yield_level" target="china_eu_auto_rivalry::cross_border_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long‑term bond yields raise the benchmark cost of capital and borrowing costs for OEMs and suppliers, causing planned cross‑border greenfield investments and factory expansions between China and the EU to be scaled back or delayed.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_ai</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_auto_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_ai::bond_yield_level" target="global_energy_diesel::refinery_utilization" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long‑term bond yields increase refiners' cost of capital and make financing for turnarounds, upgrades, and merchant crude purchases more expensive, prompting deferred maintenance/operational cutbacks and a reduction in refinery throughput rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_ai</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_diesel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_ai::bond_yield_level" target="mideast_houthi_campaign::aviation_service_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long‑term bond yields raise carriers' and lessors' financing and lease costs and increase required risk premia, prompting airlines to trim marginal routes, reduce frequencies, or suspend services into higher‑risk regions, thus lowering regional aviation service levels.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_ai</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_houthi_campaign</data>
</edge>
